! How Chinese characters are constructed

Modern simplified and traditional characters can include ''semantic components'' (indicating a meaning domain) and ''phonetic components'' (historical sound clues). The indexing radical is not necessarily the sole semantic contribution.

Character components frequently diverge in pronunciation over time. A memorable story about a glyph can help learning, but it does not establish historical etymology.

Compare [[Character/妈]], [[Character/剑]], and [[Character/语]]. Each notes the role of components. Chinese characters are traditionally called 汉字 (Hànzì); Japanese kanji use related characters.


